"primarySubject":"Biography","secondarySubjects":["Politics & Government","History"],"confidence":"high","rationale":"The book is a biography of Charles De Gaulle that focuses on his life and political influence, making Biography the primary subject, while Politics & Government and History are relevant secondary themes due to his significant role in shaping modern France.","method":"llm","model":"gpt-4o-mini","reviewStatus":"generated","inputHash":"f9ff0e0fad909d65142d5aaefa7eeb0e737758386d7ce88ec1dcf025e9006bec","summary":"But through sheer force of personality and bloody-mindedness he managed to have France recognised as one of the victorious Allies, occupying its own zone in defeated Germany. For ten years after 1958 he was President of France's Fifth Republic, which he created and which endures to this day. His pursuit of 'a certain idea of France' challenged American hegemony, took France out of NATO and twice vetoed British entry into the European Community. His controversial decolonization of Algeria brought France to the brink of civil war and provoked several assassination attempts. Julian Jackson's magnificent biography reveals this the life of this titanic figure as never before. It draws on a vast range of published and unpublished memoirs and documents - including the recently opened de Gaulle archives - to show how de Gaulle achieved so much during the War when his resources were so astonishingly few, and how, as President, he put a medium-rank power at the centre of world affairs. .","publicationYear":2018,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","label":"France","sourceId":"source-google-books-summary-a-certain-idea-of-france-the-life-of-charles-de-gaulle-julian-jackson"}],"displaySummary":"For ten years after 1958 he was President of France's Fifth Republic, which he created and which endures to this day. His pursuit of 'a certain idea of France' challenged American hegemony, took France out of NATO and twice ve